AI. Like,

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.960
instead of doing a four set,

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.540
four hours Google search session for gathering

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.620
research and compiling it, you can have it.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.420
Dude, that's, that's a really powerful use of

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.840
AI that, um, doesn't necessarily,

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.170
I think there's a lot more benefit there than

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.890
there's, uh, than what it takes away.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:58.310
Um,

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.890
versus other cases like actually writing the

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.670
paper. Yeah.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.110
Maybe for a first draft, but I think.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.970
makes more, there's a lot more benefit for the

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.910
user, the lab assistant to,

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.650
um, do that themselves and then have AI as an

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.120
assistant to help facilitate writing.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:16.740
Um,

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:18.740
and so I think, I think you're totally right

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.500
with that and making that the lab culture, of

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.000
making that the understanding when people come

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.300
and this is how we use AI.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.820
Yeah, and that helps you like get the background

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.540
to do their research because like,

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.060
it's giving you information.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.600
It's not doing the research for you.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.160
Like, you're not going to be publishing on what

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:34.940
already exists.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.700
So I don't see any problem in using it to learn

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.270
as long as that doesn't go into,

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.650
okay, now Claude, do all this research from

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.570
all these tests, interpret it, and then do something

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.030
based off of what you learned.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.220
I guess it's kind of what Beijing optimization

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.660
is like it learns from

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.520
past information. Mm -hmm.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:02:59.960
That'll be a closed loop.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:00.460
Yeah.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.700
But again, like, making sure that we understand

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.060
everything that goes on and we interpret it as

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.680
well, and give our own ideas instead of,

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.950
okay, Claude, here's,

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.290
like, I don't have any ideas, just do whatever

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.750
you think is best. Maybe

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.810
making up the culture to actually put in some

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.870
effort, okay, I need to, I need to give it some

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.890
ideas that I've thought of myself.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.650
Yeah. And then have it,

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.870
give it that, and then have it, um,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.520
extrapolate. Yeah, have a critique your ideas.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:32.060
Like, yeah,

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.540
give it a baseline. Like, here's what I'm thinking.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.680
Is there something wrong with what I'm thinking?

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.400
How could this be improved.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.940
And then once it gives you those, like,

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:42.980
criticisms,

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.420
see, okay, is what it's telling me I can do better,

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.960
actually going to make it better, or are there

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.660
problems with what I see that it's doing?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.600
And that'll help you think as well while while

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.280
you're using AI.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:54.340
Yeah, I agree.
